{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe live Jira DC harness cell `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_store_copy_isolation.py::test_the_store_copy_is_complete_and_scrubbed` FAILS on current origin/main:\n\n    AssertionError: binding/snapshot artifacts survived the scrub: ['.bridge_state']\n\nObserved in the 'jira DC harness smoke' job of Live External Integration run 31807853902 (job 94790999602), 2026-08-14, against origin/main. The J11 store-copy fixture scrubs `.bridge_state*` from the copied store, but the artifact survives into the copy the isolation cell asserts is fully scrubbed, muddying the live DC signal for unrelated work.\n\n## Root cause (regression origin)\nThe `dc_store_copy_repo` fixture (`tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_fixtures.py`) scrubs `.bridge_state*`, commits, and THEN calls `run_ensures()` to converge the `git archive` copy into a writable store. Commit 72731d3745 (2026-08-13, ticket 462d / epic 0303) added the `projects-seed` ensure unit (`rebar._store.project_ensures.seed_projects_mapping_unit`), which unconditionally re-creates and COMMITS `.bridge_state/projects.json` whenever its tree-check (`git show tickets:.bridge_state/projects.json`) misses — which is exactly the state the scrub leaves. That seed unit post-dates the J11 scrub (2026-08-07), so converging the copy silently resurrects the cache the scrub had removed. Before epic 0303, `run_ensures` created nothing under `.bridge_state`, so the scrub held.\n\n## Approach\nExtract the scrub into a small module-level helper `scrub_bridge_state(tracker, *, commit=False)` in `_dc_fixtures.py` (glob-matched, as before). Call it in the original position, and AGAIN after `run_ensures` converges the store — this second pass commits the removal so the `projects-seed` unit's resurrected `.bridge_state/projects.json` is removed from both the worktree and the tickets tree. This is a principled fix (re-scrub the whole `.bridge_state*` glob after convergence) rather than special-casing one filename, and it keeps the `.env-id` store marker that `run_ensures` creates intact.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_fixtures.py` — add `scrub_bridge_state` helper; re-scrub after `run_ensures`.\n- `tests/unit/test_dc_store_copy_fetch_diagnostics.py` — add a fast repo-tier regression test: the `projects-seed` unit resurrects `.bridge_state/projects.json`, and the committing re-scrub removes it (worktree + tickets tree).\n\n## Testing\n- Fast unit test (`TestBridgeStateScrub`) drives the real `seed_projects_mapping_unit` to reproduce the resurrection (negative control) and asserts the post-converge scrub leaves no `.bridge_state*` and a clean git tree — no live harness needed.\n- The live cell `test_the_store_copy_is_complete_and_scrubbed` is the ultimate check; it runs in the operator-dispatched DC-harness job (~1h), not a per-commit gate.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The store-copy scrub removes `.bridge_state` (and any equivalent binding/snapshot cache) so `test_the_store_copy_is_complete_and_scrubbed` passes in the live DC-harness job — verified by the re-scrub after `run_ensures` and the fast unit regression test in `tests/unit/test_dc_store_copy_fetch_diagnostics.py` (Gerrit change 1783 / commit 716454cbe5, merged). [operator-attested] live DC-harness confirmation is deferred to the operator's next dispatched run.\n- [x] A root-cause note explains why `.bridge_state` began surviving the scrub (regression origin) — recorded in this description (## Root cause) and as a ticket comment.\n\n## Notes\nIndependent of the rich-text epic (vigilant-erasable-pony); does NOT touch `test_dc_rich_text_live.py` (owned concurrently by graywolf-land)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786732378318852001,"uuid":"f891804b-1341-4bdd-9126-2f53b2fd0113"}